 ### [Gaussian Representation and Truncation](12855-gaussian-representation-and-truncation.md)
-This article defines the fundamental data structure and rendering primitives used in 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) and its variants. It specifies how a scene is represented as a set of $N$ learnable 3D Gaussians, detailing the parameters (position, rotation, scale, opacity, color), the construction of the covariance matrix, and the projection to 2D for rasterization. It also defines the standard truncation logic used to optimize rendering speed by discarding fragments with negligible contribution. This representation serves as the foundation for all sibling methods in the [Scene Representation and Geometry Constraints](15421-scene-representation-and-geometry-constraints.md) family and the child methods listed below. [Gaussian Representation and Truncation](12855-gaussian-representation-and-truncation.md)
