 ### [Mesh Extraction and Representation](14095-mesh-extraction-and-representation.md)
-This family of methods converts the volumetric, implicit representation of 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) into explicit geometric structures, primarily triangular meshes or point clouds, to enable compatibility with standard 3D graphics pipelines, editing tools, and animation systems. Unlike standard 3DGS, which renders via alpha-composited splats, these methods extract a discrete surface or point set that approximates the scene geometry. [SuGaR Mesh Extraction](12580-sugar-mesh-extraction.md) achieves this by regularizing Gaussians to align with the surface during training, while [3D Gaussian Splatting to Point Cloud](14068-3d-gaussian-splatting-to-point-cloud.md) samples points from the Gaussian distribution post-training. [Mesh Extraction and Representation](14095-mesh-extraction-and-representation.md)
